  "reading": "ひきさげる",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to lower, to reduce, to cut",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to lower, to reduce",
      "explanation": "To decrease a price, rate, level, or standard."
    },
    {
      "sense_number": 2,
      "gloss": "to withdraw, to pull back",
      "explanation": "To withdraw troops, people, or proposals."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "06193_hikisageru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{価格|かかく}を{引|ひ}き{下|さ}げる。",
      "english": "Lower the price.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06193_hikisageru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{政府|せいふ}は{消費税|しょうひぜい}を{引|ひ}き{下|さ}げた。",
      "english": "The government lowered the consumption tax.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06193_hikisageru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{金利|きんり}を{大幅|おおはば}に{引|ひ}き{下|さ}げることで、{景気|けいき}を{刺激|しげき}しようとしている。",
      "english": "They are trying to stimulate the economy by significantly lowering interest rates.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06193_hikisageru_ex4",
      "japanese": "{提案|ていあん}を{引|ひ}き{下|さ}げるしかない。",
      "english": "We have no choice but to withdraw the proposal.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06193_hikisageru_ex5",
      "japanese": "{部隊|ぶたい}を{前線|ぜんせん}から{引|ひ}き{下|さ}げた。",
      "english": "The troops were pulled back from the front line.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06193_hikisageru_ex6",
      "japanese": "{反対|はんたい}が{強|つよ}かったため、{法案|ほうあん}を{引|ひ}き{下|さ}げることになった。",
      "english": "Due to strong opposition, the bill had to be withdrawn.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: Transitive ({他動詞|たどうし})\n\nINTRANSITIVE PAIR: {引|ひ}き{下|さ}がる (to step back, to withdraw)\n\nASPECT: {引|ひ}き{下|さ}げている can indicate an ongoing price reduction or a state of having reduced something.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n・{価格|かかく}を{引|ひ}き{下|さ}げる (to lower the price)\n・{金利|きんり}を{引|ひ}き{下|さ}げる (to lower interest rates)\n・{税率|ぜいりつ}を{引|ひ}き{下|さ}げる (to lower the tax rate)\n・{水準|すいじゅん}を{引|ひ}き{下|さ}げる (to lower the standard)\n・{提案|ていあん}を{引|ひ}き{下|さ}げる (to withdraw a proposal)\n\nANTONYM: {引|ひ}き{上|あ}げる (to raise, to pull up)\n\nNOTE: Often used in business, economic, and political contexts.",
